A hold reserves a **title**, not a particular copy. Holds queue first come, first served.

**Turn it on:** **Library Settings → Holds** (**Let borrowers reserve books**).

## What happens

1. A borrower reserves a book that is out. The desk can do this with **Reserve a book**; parents and
   students can too if the portal allows it, and teachers from [My Library](/docs/educonnect-library-my-library).
2. When a copy is checked in it goes to the oldest waiting hold and sits on the **hold shelf**. Put
   it physically aside.
3. The borrower has **School days to collect** (default 3) to pick it up. Lending it to them fulfils
   the hold. An uncollected hold expires and the copy moves to the next in the queue or back to the
   shelf.

A copy on the hold shelf lends only to the borrower it is held for unless an override is used. A book
with waiting holds is not renewed.

Each borrower may have a limited number of holds (**Holds per borrower**, default 2; 0 means only the
desk places holds).

## The Holds page

**Library → Holds** shows the **Hold shelf** (books set aside and who for) and the queues. Anyone with
**Place & cancel holds for borrowers** can cancel.
